    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Twisted right ankle playing football yesterday. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Marley was seen the same day after twisting his right ankle in a five-a-side football game yesterday evening, seven and a half weeks after the excision of his right great toe nail unit. He went over on the outside of the ankle when he landed from a header. He felt pain on the outer side, swelling came up within an hour, and he walked off with a limp. He iced and raised it overnight. He can walk on it with a limp. He did not hit or stub the operated toe and the graft does not hurt. The surgical team cleared him to return to football at the six-week graft check two weeks ago, and wears the stiff-soled shoe for daily walking but played in ordinary football boots. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Yesterday evening, an inversion injury landing at football</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Outer side of the right ankle</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Pain 5 of 10; walks with a limp</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Seven and a half weeks after digit-sparing surgery to the right great toe; cleared for football two weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Ice and elevation help; worse on turning the foot in</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Swelling; no numbness, no pain in the toe or graft, no pain in the groin</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Right lateral ankle pain and swelling; no knee or foot pain</td></tr><tr><td>Integumentary</td><td>Negative</td><td>Graft on the right great toe intact and painless; no new skin changes</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Negative</td><td>No numbness or tingling in the foot</td></tr><tr><td>Hematologic and lymphatic</td><td>Negative</td><td>No groin swelling or lump</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

